# VibeTune build banner (`Source/Apps/VibeTune/vibetune.asm`)

Whenever you produce or refresh **`vtune.com`**, do **both** of the following **before** running **`Source/Apps/VibeTune/Build.cmd`**:

## 1. Bump the debug build number only (every build)

- Update **`#DEFINE VTBANREL "bNNN"`** only (one token: leading **`b`** + incrementing build number).
- **`VTBANREL` must not carry the software revision.** It is only the rolling debug/build counter.
- **Software revision** stays **`0.1`** until the user explicitly requests a revision change. That revision lives as the literal **`v0.1`** in **`MSGBAN`** (`.DB` **`"…RomWBW v0.1"`** then **`VTBANREL`**, e.g. printed **`v0.1b145`**).
- **`VTBANREL`** is also expanded in the **PT3 ident** string (`...Player r.` + token + `=`).

Do **not** add scripts or generated `.inc` files for versioning unless the user explicitly asks for that.

## 2. Banner date = machine “today”, not chat metadata

- **Never** trust Cursor’s injected “Today’s date” / session metadata for the banner string.
- **Do** use the actual calendar date on the user’s machine (e.g. `Get-Date -Format 'dd-MMM-yyyy'` in PowerShell) in **`MSGBAN`** after the comma (e.g. `…v0.1b145, 14-May-2026`).

If the shell date is unavailable or ambiguous, ask the user for the date string to embed.

## Workspace note

When the Cursor workspace root is **`Source/Apps/VibeTune`**, the same policy is in **`Source/Apps/VibeTune/.cursor/rules/vibetune-build-banner.mdc`** with **`alwaysApply: true`**.
